{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function useDebouncedState<TValue, TSelected>(\n   value,\n   options,\n   selector?): [TValue, Dispatch<StateUpdater<TValue>>, PreactDebouncer<Dispatch<StateUpdater<TValue>>, TSelected>];","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/preact-pacer/src/debouncer/useDebouncedState.ts#L79","children":[{"type":"text","value":"debouncer/useDebouncedState.ts:79"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A Preact hook that creates a debounced state value, combining Preact's useState with debouncing functionality.\nThis hook provides both the current debounced value and methods to update it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The state value is only updated after the specified wait time has elapsed since the last update attempt.\nIf another update is attempted before the wait time expires, the timer resets and starts waiting again.\nThis is useful for handling frequent state updates that should be throttled, like search input values\nor window resize dimensions."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The hook returns a tuple containing:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The current debounced value"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A function to update the debounced value"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The debouncer instance with additional control methods"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"state-management-and-selector","children":[{"type":"text","value":"State Management and Selector"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The hook uses TanStack Store for reactive state management via the underlying debouncer instance.\nThe "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"selector"},{"type":"text","value":" parameter allows you to specify which debouncer state changes will trigger a re-render,\noptimizing performance by preventing unnecessary re-renders when irrelevant state changes occur."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By default, there will be no reactive state subscriptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and you must opt-in to state\ntracking by providing a selector function. This prevents unnecessary re-renders and gives you\nfull control over when your component updates. Only when you provide a selector will the\ncomponent re-render when the selected state values change."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Available debouncer state properties:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"canLeadingExecute"},{"type":"text","value":": Whether the debouncer can execute on the leading edge"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"executionCount"},{"type":"text","value":": Number of function executions that have been completed"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isPending"},{"type":"text","value":": Whether the debouncer is waiting for the timeout to trigger execution"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lastArgs"},{"type":"text","value":": The arguments from the most recent call to maybeExecute"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"status"},{"type":"text","value":": Current execution status ('disabled' | 'idle' | 'pending')"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tvalue","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TValue"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tselected","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TSelected"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":" = "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DebouncerState"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Dispatch"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"StateUpdater"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"},{"type":"text","value":">>>"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"value","children":[{"type":"text","value":"value"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/PreactDebouncerOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"PreactDebouncerOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Dispatch"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"StateUpdater"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"},{"type":"text","value":">>, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"selector","children":[{"type":"text","value":"selector?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state"},{"type":"text","value":") => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"["},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Dispatch"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"StateUpdater"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"},{"type":"text","value":">>, "},{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/PreactDebouncer.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"PreactDebouncer"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Dispatch"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"StateUpdater"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"},{"type":"text","value":">>, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":">]"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Default behavior - no reactive state subscriptions\nconst [searchTerm, setSearchTerm, debouncer] = useDebouncedState('', {\n  wait: 500 // Wait 500ms after last keystroke\n});\n\n// Opt-in to re-render when pending state changes (optimized for loading indicators)\nconst [searchTerm, setSearchTerm, debouncer] = useDebouncedState(\n  '',\n  { wait: 500 },\n  (state) => ({ isPending: state.isPending })\n);\n\n// Opt-in to re-render when execution count changes (optimized for tracking executions)\nconst [searchTerm, setSearchTerm, debouncer] = useDebouncedState(\n  '',\n  { wait: 500 },\n  (state) => ({ executionCount: state.executionCount })\n);\n\n// Opt-in to re-render when debouncing status changes (optimized for status display)\nconst [searchTerm, setSearchTerm, debouncer] = useDebouncedState(\n  '',\n  { wait: 500 },\n  (state) => ({\n    status: state.status,\n    canLeadingExecute: state.canLeadingExecute\n  })\n);\n\n// Update value - will be debounced\nconst handleChange = (e) => {\n  setSearchTerm(e.target.value);\n};\n\n// Access the selected debouncer state (will be empty object {} unless selector provided)\nconst { isPending, executionCount } = debouncer.state;","lang":"tsx"}],"headings":[{"id":"state-management-and-selector","text":"State Management and Selector","level":2},{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tvalue","text":"TValue","level":3},{"id":"tselected","text":"TSelected","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"value","text":"value","level":3},{"id":"options","text":"options","level":3},{"id":"selector","text":"selector?","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction useDebouncedState<TValue, TSelected>(\n   value,\n   options,\n   selector?): [TValue, Dispatch<StateUpdater<TValue>>, PreactDebouncer<Dispatch<StateUpdater<TValue>>, TSelected>];\n```\n\nDefined in: [debouncer/useDebouncedState.ts:79](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/preact-pacer/src/debouncer/useDebouncedState.ts#L79)\n\nA Preact hook that creates a debounced state value, combining Preact's useState with debouncing functionality.\nThis hook provides both the current debounced value and methods to update it.\n\nThe state value is only updated after the specified wait time has elapsed since the last update attempt.\nIf another update is attempted before the wait time expires, the timer resets and starts waiting again.\nThis is useful for handling frequent state updates that should be throttled, like search input values\nor window resize dimensions.\n\nThe hook returns a tuple containing:\n- The current debounced value\n- A function to update the debounced value\n- The debouncer instance with additional control methods\n\n## State Management and Selector\n\nThe hook uses TanStack Store for reactive state management via the underlying debouncer instance.\nThe `selector` parameter allows you to specify which debouncer state changes will trigger a re-render,\noptimizing performance by preventing unnecessary re-renders when irrelevant state changes occur.\n\n**By default, there will be no reactive state subscriptions** and you must opt-in to state\ntracking by providing a selector function. This prevents unnecessary re-renders and gives you\nfull control over when your component updates. Only when you provide a selector will the\ncomponent re-render when the selected state values change.\n\nAvailable debouncer state properties:\n- `canLeadingExecute`: Whether the debouncer can execute on the leading edge\n- `executionCount`: Number of function executions that have been completed\n- `isPending`: Whether the debouncer is waiting for the timeout to trigger execution\n- `lastArgs`: The arguments from the most recent call to maybeExecute\n- `status`: Current execution status ('disabled' | 'idle' | 'pending')\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TValue\n\n`TValue`\n\n### TSelected\n\n`TSelected` = `DebouncerState`\\<`Dispatch`\\<`StateUpdater`\\<`TValue`\\>\\>\\>\n\n## Parameters\n\n### value\n\n`TValue`\n\n### options\n\n[`PreactDebouncerOptions`](../interfaces/PreactDebouncerOptions.md)\\<`Dispatch`\\<`StateUpdater`\\<`TValue`\\>\\>, `TSelected`\\>\n\n### selector?\n\n(`state`) => `TSelected`\n\n## Returns\n\n\\[`TValue`, `Dispatch`\\<`StateUpdater`\\<`TValue`\\>\\>, [`PreactDebouncer`](../interfaces/PreactDebouncer.md)\\<`Dispatch`\\<`StateUpdater`\\<`TValue`\\>\\>, `TSelected`\\>\\]\n\n## Example\n\n```tsx\n// Default behavior - no reactive state subscriptions\nconst [searchTerm, setSearchTerm, debouncer] = useDebouncedState('', {\n  wait: 500 // Wait 500ms after last keystroke\n});\n\n// Opt-in to re-render when pending state changes (optimized for loading indicators)\nconst [searchTerm, setSearchTerm, debouncer] = useDebouncedState(\n  '',\n  { wait: 500 },\n  (state) => ({ isPending: state.isPending })\n);\n\n// Opt-in to re-render when execution count changes (optimized for tracking executions)\nconst [searchTerm, setSearchTerm, debouncer] = useDebouncedState(\n  '',\n  { wait: 500 },\n  (state) => ({ executionCount: state.executionCount })\n);\n\n// Opt-in to re-render when debouncing status changes (optimized for status display)\nconst [searchTerm, setSearchTerm, debouncer] = useDebouncedState(\n  '',\n  { wait: 500 },\n  (state) => ({\n    status: state.status,\n    canLeadingExecute: state.canLeadingExecute\n  })\n);\n\n// Update value - will be debounced\nconst handleChange = (e) => {\n  setSearchTerm(e.target.value);\n};\n\n// Access the selected debouncer state (will be empty object {} unless selector provided)\nconst { isPending, executionCount } = debouncer.state;\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: useDebouncedState\ntitle: useDebouncedState\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction useDebouncedState<TValue, TSelected>(\n   value,\n   options,\n   selector?): [TValue, Dispatch<StateUpdater<TValue>>, PreactDebouncer<Dispatch<StateUpdater<TValue>>, TSelected>];\n```\n\nDefined in: [debouncer/useDebouncedState.ts:79](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/preact-pacer/src/debouncer/useDebouncedState.ts#L79)\n\nA Preact hook that creates a debounced state value, combining Preact's useState with debouncing functionality.\nThis hook provides both the current debounced value and methods to update it.\n\nThe state value is only updated after the specified wait time has elapsed since the last update attempt.\nIf another update is attempted before the wait time expires, the timer resets and starts waiting again.\nThis is useful for handling frequent state updates that should be throttled, like search input values\nor window resize dimensions.\n\nThe hook returns a tuple containing:\n- The current debounced value\n- A function to update the debounced value\n- The debouncer instance with additional control methods\n\n## State Management and Selector\n\nThe hook uses TanStack Store for reactive state management via the underlying debouncer instance.\nThe `selector` parameter allows you to specify which debouncer state changes will trigger a re-render,\noptimizing performance by preventing unnecessary re-renders when irrelevant state changes occur.\n\n**By default, there will be no reactive state subscriptions** and you must opt-in to state\ntracking by providing a selector function. This prevents unnecessary re-renders and gives you\nfull control over when your component updates. Only when you provide a selector will the\ncomponent re-render when the selected state values change.\n\nAvailable debouncer state properties:\n- `canLeadingExecute`: Whether the debouncer can execute on the leading edge\n- `executionCount`: Number of function executions that have been completed\n- `isPending`: Whether the debouncer is waiting for the timeout to trigger execution\n- `lastArgs`: The arguments from the most recent call to maybeExecute\n- `status`: Current execution status ('disabled' | 'idle' | 'pending')\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TValue\n\n`TValue`\n\n### TSelected\n\n`TSelected` = `DebouncerState`\\<`Dispatch`\\<`StateUpdater`\\<`TValue`\\>\\>\\>\n\n## Parameters\n\n### value\n\n`TValue`\n\n### options\n\n[`PreactDebouncerOptions`](../interfaces/PreactDebouncerOptions.md)\\<`Dispatch`\\<`StateUpdater`\\<`TValue`\\>\\>, `TSelected`\\>\n\n### selector?\n\n(`state`) => `TSelected`\n\n## Returns\n\n\\[`TValue`, `Dispatch`\\<`StateUpdater`\\<`TValue`\\>\\>, [`PreactDebouncer`](../interfaces/PreactDebouncer.md)\\<`Dispatch`\\<`StateUpdater`\\<`TValue`\\>\\>, `TSelected`\\>\\]\n\n## Example\n\n```tsx\n// Default behavior - no reactive state subscriptions\nconst [searchTerm, setSearchTerm, debouncer] = useDebouncedState('', {\n  wait: 500 // Wait 500ms after last keystroke\n});\n\n// Opt-in to re-render when pending state changes (optimized for loading indicators)\nconst [searchTerm, setSearchTerm, debouncer] = useDebouncedState(\n  '',\n  { wait: 500 },\n  (state) => ({ isPending: state.isPending })\n);\n\n// Opt-in to re-render when execution count changes (optimized for tracking executions)\nconst [searchTerm, setSearchTerm, debouncer] = useDebouncedState(\n  '',\n  { wait: 500 },\n  (state) => ({ executionCount: state.executionCount })\n);\n\n// Opt-in to re-render when debouncing status changes (optimized for status display)\nconst [searchTerm, setSearchTerm, debouncer] = useDebouncedState(\n  '',\n  { wait: 500 },\n  (state) => ({\n    status: state.status,\n    canLeadingExecute: state.canLeadingExecute\n  })\n);\n\n// Update value - will be debounced\nconst handleChange = (e) => {\n  setSearchTerm(e.target.value);\n};\n\n// Access the selected debouncer state (will be empty object {} unless selector provided)\nconst { isPending, executionCount } = debouncer.state;\n```\n"}
